# Story: As a security officer, I want repeated failed sign-ins to lock an account for a while, so that passwords cannot be guessed by trying many of them. After five failed sign-ins for one username within fifteen minutes, sign-in for that username is refused for five minutes with TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS, even with the right password. Other accounts are not affected.

@draft
Feature: Account Lockout After Multiple Failed Login Attempts

  Scenario Outline: Five failed login attempts lock an account for five minutes
    Given a user has attempted to log in with the wrong password four times within fifteen minutes
    When they attempt to log in again with the correct password
    Then the system refuses their sign-in and displays TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS

    Examples:
      | username |

  Scenario: Correct login after account unlock period
    Given a user has attempted to log in with the wrong password five times within fifteen minutes
    And it is now five minutes past the last failed attempt time
    When they attempt to log in again with the correct password
    Then the system allows their sign-in and logs them in successfully

  Scenario: Other accounts are not affected by a locked account
    Given another user has never attempted to log in or has not reached too many attempts
    When that other user attempts to log in with the correct password
    Then the system allows their sign-in and logs them in successfully
